10
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:37,160
After a sample comes in contact with a crystal, light is sent into the crystal below a certain angle, known as the critical angle.

11
00:00:37,760 --> 00:00:43,300
When the light is kept at or below this angle, it bounces through the crystal and is collected on the other side.

12
00:00:44,260 --> 00:00:48,960
Information about the sample is gathered through the interaction of an evanescent wave and the sample.

13
00:00:49,540 --> 00:00:54,960
This evanescent wave is a standing wave that occurs at inflection points of the propagating light.

14
00:00:54,960 --> 00:01:00,360
After interaction with the sample, it carries the chemical information along with it to the detector.

15
00:01:01,060 --> 00:01:08,520
This evanescent wave is key to how ATR is able to provide the user vibrational or chemical information about the sample of interest.

16
